        "file": "Dockerfile",
        "lang": "dockerfile",
        "kind": "secure",
        "code": "# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1\n\n# ---- Build stage: tools needed to install dependencies stay here ----\nFROM python:3.13-slim AS build\nWORKDIR /app\n# Copy only the dependency list first: better layer caching, nothing unexpected copied\nCOPY requirements.txt .\n# requirements.txt pins exact versions; --no-cache-dir keeps the layer small\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir --prefix=/install -r requirements.txt\n\n# ---- Runtime stage: minimal image, no build tools ----\nFROM python:3.13-slim\n# Dedicated unprivileged user with a fixed numeric UID\nRUN groupadd --system --gid 10001 app \\\n    && useradd --system --uid 10001 --gid app --no-create-home app\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY --from=build /install /usr/local\n# Copy only what the application needs, owned by the unprivileged user\nCOPY --chown=app:app app.py .\n\n# Numeric UID so Kubernetes can verify runAsNonRoot\nUSER 10001\n# Unprivileged port (above 1024)\nEXPOSE 8000\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s \\\n  CMD [\"python\", \"-c\", \"import urllib.request; urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/health')\"]\n# Exec form: the app is PID 1 and receives SIGTERM directly\nCMD [\"python\", \"app.py\"]\n",
        "output": "$ docker build -t app:1.0.0 .\n$ docker run --rm app:1.0.0 id\nuid=10001(app) gid=10001(app) groups=10001(app)\n",
        "note": {
          "fr": "Les points à citer à voix haute : image de base versionnée et minimale, build multi-étapes, aucun secret, utilisateur non root avec UID numérique, forme exec pour `CMD`. Ajoutez un `.dockerignore` (`.git`, `.env`, `*.pem`) et, en production, l'épinglage de l'image de base par digest.",
          "en": "The points to say out loud: versioned minimal base image, multi-stage build, no secret, non-root user with a numeric UID, exec form for `CMD`. Add a `.dockerignore` (`.git`, `.env`, `*.pem`) and, in production, pin the base image by digest."
        }
