    "exercise": {
      "statement": {
        "fr": "Question classique : « Donnez à l'application de supervision un accès en **lecture seule** aux Pods\ndu namespace `shop`, et rien d'autre. »\n\n1. Créez un ServiceAccount `monitor` dans le namespace `shop`.\n2. Créez un Role `pod-reader` autorisant `get`, `list` et `watch` sur les Pods et leurs journaux.\n3. Liez le Role au ServiceAccount avec un RoleBinding.\n4. Donnez les deux commandes `kubectl auth can-i` qui prouvent que `monitor` peut lister les Pods\n   mais ne peut pas lire les Secrets.\n",
        "en": "A classic question: \"Give the monitoring application **read-only** access to the Pods of the\n`shop` namespace, and nothing else.\"\n\n1. Create a ServiceAccount `monitor` in the `shop` namespace.\n2. Create a Role `pod-reader` allowing `get`, `list` and `watch` on Pods and their logs.\n3. Bind the Role to the ServiceAccount with a RoleBinding.\n4. Give the two `kubectl auth can-i` commands proving that `monitor` can list Pods but cannot read\n   Secrets.\n"
      },
      "solution": {
        "file": "rbac-pod-reader.yaml",
        "lang": "yaml",
        "code": "apiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: monitor\n  namespace: shop\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Role\nmetadata:\n  name: pod-reader\n  namespace: shop\nrules:\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"] # \"\" is the core API group (pods, services, secrets...)\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"pods/log\"]\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"] # read-only verbs, no wildcard\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: RoleBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: monitor-pod-reader\n  namespace: shop\nsubjects:\n  - kind: ServiceAccount\n    name: monitor\n    namespace: shop\nroleRef:\n  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io\n  kind: Role\n  name: pod-reader\n# Verification:\n#   kubectl auth can-i list pods   -n shop --as=system:serviceaccount:shop:monitor   -> yes\n#   kubectl auth can-i get secrets -n shop --as=system:serviceaccount:shop:monitor   -> no\n",
        "note": {
          "fr": "Un Role et un RoleBinding (et non un ClusterRole lié par ClusterRoleBinding) limitent l'accès au seul namespace `shop`. Le sujet d'un ServiceAccount s'écrit `system:serviceaccount:<namespace>:<nom>`.",
          "en": "A Role and a RoleBinding (not a ClusterRole bound with a ClusterRoleBinding) restrict access to the `shop` namespace only. A ServiceAccount subject is written `system:serviceaccount:<namespace>:<name>`."
        }
      }
    },
